    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "The incident summary",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Close the report with the paragraph an on-call engineer would paste into the incident channel.",
        "",
        "1. Add the extension method `ServerErrors(this IEnumerable<Entry> entries)` that keeps statuses of 500 and above.",
        "2. After the sessions, print an empty line, then either `Incident: none`, or these four lines:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Incident: N server errors from HH:mm:ss to HH:mm:ss",
        "Error rate: X.X%",
        "Worst endpoint: endpoint (K errors)",
        "Affected IPs: ip, ip",
        "```",
        "",
        "- The times are the first and last server error, by time.",
        "- The error rate is server errors as a percentage of all parsed entries, one decimal place.",
        "- The worst endpoint has the most server errors; ties alphabetically. Use `CountBy`.",
        "- Affected IPs are distinct, alphabetical, joined with `, `.",
        "",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "2026-06-10T14:00:00 10.1.1.1 GET /api/pay 200 90ms",
        "2026-06-10T14:00:10 10.1.1.2 GET /api/pay 502 5000ms",
        "2026-06-10T14:00:11 10.1.1.3 GET /api/pay 502 5000ms",
        "2026-06-10T14:00:12 10.1.1.1 PUT /api/cart 500 40ms",
        "2026-06-10T14:00:15 10.1.1.2 PUT /api/cart 500 41ms",
        "2026-06-10T14:00:20 10.1.1.2 GET /api/pay 200 95ms",
        "broken",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Parsed: 6, skipped: 1",
